## 20. MVP Definition of Done

The MVP is "done" when a new player can:

1. Wake up in the apartment, learn the basic loop in their first in-game day
2. Grow weed from seed to harvest over an in-game week
3. Sell stolen goods to the Fence
4. Buy supplies from the Hardware Store
5. Receive a page, return the call, complete a deal, get paid at retail
6. Develop a recurring buyer relationship over multiple successful deals
7. Loot at least one car successfully
8. Reach Tier 1 in each XP track (DealerExperience, CriminalExperience)
9. Develop one player skill to a meaningful threshold and feel the capability change (e.g., vault unlock)
10. Build relationship with at least one of the 6 NPCs to a meaningful threshold
11. Hang out with an NPC, choosing it over a competing income opportunity
12. Get caught committing a minor crime and pay the fine
13. Encounter at least one scripted event, triggered by skill or relationship gating
14. Survive (or fail to survive) a full in-game month including rent obligations
15. Save and reload without state loss

If all fifteen are achievable in a vertical slice, MVP is done and "is this loop fun?" can be answered with real playtest data.

